// ---- Storage arithmetic ---------------------------------------------------
// A real migration filled a 25 GB root disk to 92% and two of three compose
// projects died with `no space left on device`, because the pre-flight only
// counted the ~11 GB file copy. Docker needs FAR more than the image bytes:
// `docker load`/`docker pull` writes the compressed stream, the content store
// (/var/lib/containerd/io.containerd.content.v1.content) keeps the layer blobs
// AND the snapshotter unpacks them again, and any `build` adds a build cache on
// top (measured: `docker builder prune -af` reclaimed 7.1 GB right after two
// image builds). So the allowance is 2× the source's image bytes plus a fixed
// floor, and free space is re-checked immediately before the image phase and
// again before every single image — never just once at the start.
